msgid "ArduPilot has FrSky telemetry drivers to natively output autopilot information through the serial ports. It comes in two flavors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-protocol-info.rst:18
#: 496ee2389a6e44da8012b8291f22275a
msgid ":ref:`Repurposed FrSky telemetry <common-frsky-repurposed>` (D and SmartPort), which reuses FrSky data IDs to transmit basic flight control information to the RC transmitter (e.g. T2 temperature message reused to transmit the number of GPS satellites and GPS status); and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-protocol-info.rst:20
#: e5e06338d1194ce2b3ca48221c31b864
msgid ":ref:`Passthrough telemetry <common-frsky-passthrough>` (SmartPort), which leverages the new passthrough FrSky data IDs to send an extensive amount of autopilot specific information to the RC transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-protocol-info.rst:22
#: f2cb34bc27b646308ee5185b188ab505
msgid "FrSky telemetry is also possible through the use of a :ref:`MAVLink to FrSky converter <common-frsky-mavlink>`."
msgstr ""

